{"year":"2025","content":[{"type":"text","content_text":"The 82nd ceremony was held on January 5, 2025, at the Beverly Hilton, broadcast by CBS and hosted by <a href=\"https://_{type: 'screen', 'id': 552243, 'screen_type': person}\">Nikki Glaser</a>, the first woman to host the show solo. <a href=\"https://_{type: 'screen', 'id': 974950, 'screen_type': movie}\">Emilia Pérez</a> (2024) arrived with 10 nominations, a record for a musical or comedy film, and won four awards; <a href=\"https://_{type: 'screen', 'id': 549509, 'screen_type': movie}\">The Brutalist</a> (2024) took Best Motion Picture – Drama and Director (<a href=\"https://_{type: 'screen', 'id': 55493, 'screen_type': person}\">Brady Corbet</a>). <a href=\"https://_{type: 'screen', 'id': 87335, 'screen_type': person}\">Fernanda Torres</a> won Best Actress in a Motion Picture – Drama for <a href=\"https://_{type: 'screen', 'id': 1000837, 'screen_type': movie}\">I'm Still Here</a> (2024) and became the first Brazilian to win in a Golden Globe acting category. <i>Television awards are not included.</i>"},{"type":"awards_nominees","name":"Best Motion Picture – Drama","nominee_list":[{"type":"movie","id":549509,"name":"The Brutalist","image_path":"/52iVP3AtNtpjFiBxlOYCUPXhr47.jpg","director":"Brady Corbet","winner":true,"backdrop_path":"/hmZnqijPaaACjenDkrbWcCmcADI.jpg"},{"type":"movie","id":661539,"name":"A Complete Unknown","image_path":"/tXNPJ3XvF4RaEV66Qm9QO3pu3w7.jpg","director":"James Mangold","winner":false},{"type":"movie","id":974576,"name":"Conclave","image_path":"/7pMyhSbULMkCCOQCInBYU34Qmf3.jpg","director":"Edward Berger","winner":false},{"type":"movie","id":693134,"name":"Dune: Part Two","image_path":"/VMy4UGsI2u3f4fALGeCqCdsQBb.jpg","director":"Denis Villeneuve","winner":false},{"type":"movie","id":1028196,"name":"Nickel Boys","image_path":"/hlTuZinZ2EvrkTKpW66z2RXySmE.jpg","director":"RaMell Ross","winner":false},{"type":"movie","id":1211472,"name":"September 5","image_path":"/3emldMXl1Q3p5yFUOZm